If MIN #good_j >= 1 (no fails) with big margin and maxarc*Vmax>1 across all
spreads at the WORST Vmax=s+14, the large-spread half holds: a good ruler
period always exists.  The pigeonhole #good >= rho*Vmax-#arcs then just needs
the rigorous linear arc-count bound #arcs<=c*spread with c<rho* (~0.2 observed).
